# The repo owner must review every change to the server-side write surface.
# These are the two paths that run with any privilege against user data:
# migrations alter the database schema, and edge functions run server-side.

# Database migrations are the security-critical path. A bad migration can
# rewrite RLS policies, grant roles, or drop tables — review every line.
supabase/migrations/ @jaredoka

# Edge functions run on Supabase's runtime, not on the client. The parsers
# copy under _shared/parsers is generated by scripts/sync-parsers.mjs and must
# never be hand-edited.
supabase/functions/ @jaredoka
